<title>USA: Arrow Air CEO Terence Fensome resigns.</title>
<headline>Arrow Air CEO Terence Fensome resigns.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arrow Air Inc said Tuesday Terence Fensome had resigned as president and chief executive officer of the company.</p>
<p>The company said Fensome wanted to &quot;pursue other interests&quot; without elaborating.</p>
<p>It said the board of directors had named Jonathan Batchelor, senior vice president-international sales, as acting president until it named a successor.</p>
<p>Arrow Air is an all-cargo carrier at Miami International Airport.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
</text>
